Body:
As a workaround, I edited `~/.config/opencode/opencode.json` and added this:

```json
{
  "$schema": "https://opencode.ai/config.json",
  "provider": {
    "openrouter": {
      "models": {
        "anthropic/claude-opus-4.7": {
          "name": "Claude Opus 4.7",
          "limit": {
            "context": 1000000,
            "output": 128000
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

Now I can select Opus 4.7.

Thinking is now omitted by default - https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/about-claude/models/whats-new-claude-4-7#thinking-content-omitted-by-default

I was able to re-enable this in my `opencode.json`

```json
"claude-opus-4-7": {
          "variants": {
            "low": {
              "thinking": { "type": "adaptive", "display": "summarized" },
            },
            "medium": {
              "thinking": { "type": "adaptive", "display": "summarized" },
            },
            "high": {
              "thinking": { "type": "adaptive", "display": "summarized" },
            },
            "xhigh": {
              "thinking": { "type": "adaptive", "display": "summarized" },
            },
            "max": {
              "thinking": { "type": "adaptive", "display": "summarized" },
            },
          },
          "options": {
            "thinking": { "type": "adaptive", "display": "summarized" },
          },
        },
```

Would be nice if this is baked into opencode

/oc undo last change and just make this condition also accept 5-mini:

if (model.api.id.includes("5.")) {
        return { store: false, reasoningEffort: "low" }
      }
